-- Interact/Lines (server): every spoken NPC line of the Interact system (Korean). DATA ONLY: no logic,
-- no requires. The Talk engine picks a line; this module only answers "what could this NPC say here".
--
-- Shape:   L.STYLES[style][situation] = { "variant", "variant", ... }
--   style      who is talking (a voice): citizen_polite, citizen_busan, student, grandma, tourist, worker,
--              thug_boss, thug_minion, fool (만복이), homeless_kind (광안리 김씨), homeless_grumpy (철수 할배),
--              drunk_sad (최 부장), drunk_rowdy (황 씨), cop, clerk (GS25 알바생)
--   situation  what is happening: greet_first, rumor, threat, flee_scream, cop_warn, clerk_hand ... (the full
--              list is the key set of L.STYLES.citizen_polite)
--   variants   one is picked at random; each is ONE short spoken line (<= 40 chars ideally, 60 max)
--
-- Placeholders (filled by the Talk engine; only these exist):
--   {player} how the NPC addresses the player (총각/손님/자네/어이/저기요...; Cast.CALL or the caller). It may
--            be a noun OR a bare vocative, so lines use it ONLY line-initially as a call: "{player}! ...",
--            "{player}, ...", "{player}~ ..."   {name} the NPC's own name
--   {place}  a nearby place name      {item}   a GS25 item (L.ITEMS)       {amount} money ("천 원")
--   {what}   short incident ("싸움", "폭행", "말다툼", "교통사고 날 뻔한 거")
--   {where}  where it happened ("광장 쪽", "편의점 앞")   {when} "아까" / "방금" / "조금 전"
--   {target} a third person's name (may default to "저 사람": no 씨 / 그 사람 glued to it)
--   Lines never put a particle that depends on the last syllable (은/는, 이/가, 을/를, 으로/로) right after
--   a placeholder, and never write "{where} 쪽" ({where} may already end in 쪽).
--
-- L.FALLBACK[style] = parent style. A situation missing in a style is looked up in its parent, then the
--   parent's parent ... and finally in citizen_polite, which defines EVERY situation key, archetype extras
--   included (written generically so any voice can borrow them). Styles not named by the spec chain to the
--   closest register: Busan voices (thug_boss, fool, homeless_kind) -> citizen_busan, others -> citizen_polite.
--
-- L.ITEMS = what GS25 customers order ({item}). Soju is never sold to customers in this game.
--
-- Adding a style: add L.STYLES.<key> = { <situation> = { ... }, ... } with only the situations where the
--   voice matters, then L.FALLBACK.<key> = "<closest existing style>". Adding a situation: add it to
--   citizen_polite FIRST (so every style can fall back to it), then override it where the voice matters.
-- Tone: PG-13 like Korean TV. Thugs threaten but never use slurs; homeless characters keep their dignity;
--   만복이 is a goofy, childlike, overconfident local, never the butt of disability jokes. No real brands
--   except GS25, no real people.

